WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.801
-I can't believe The Roots
are here, by the way.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:03.801
The Roots are here.
-Oh!

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.367
How are you here?

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.234
And do you all know
that you're here?

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.868
Raise your hand if you know
where you are?

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:12.868
Yeah.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.701
The Roots just came back.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.901
You crushed it on
the Grammys last night.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.234
You crushed it!
-Thank you.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:22.601
-I mean,
couldn't have gone any better.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.234
You have to be so proud.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.467
I mean, that was insane,
what you pulled off.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:29.767
How many artists were there?

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.634
-Yeah, it was like 24, 25.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.234
-50 years of hip hop.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.968
The Roots --
you told me about this

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.300
a month ago or two months ago.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.534
-And you're like,
"Dude, I need a day off."

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.367
I'm like,
"You never ask for a day off."

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.968
You're like,
"Let me tell you why.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.033
We have a really giant
opportunity."

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.901
-Yeah.
-And I was like, "Oh, my gosh.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.934
Go for it.
This is gonna be amazing."

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.367
It couldn't have gone
any better.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.801
It was electric to watch on TV.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:55.133
I loved it.
-Thank you.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.000
-They did a great job directing
and all that stuff, too.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.133
But it was so exciting.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.367
Everyone was up dancing.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.234
-Did you feel that in the room?

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:03.968
-We did.
It was electric.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:07.601
-Was it like almost
human D.J.'ing?

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.234
It's like,
"I'm gonna put this song on,

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:11.434
but they're really here."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.200
Yeah, it's like,
"I'm gonna put on Run-D.M.C.,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.067
but they're really here.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.267
I realized, like,
while we were doing it, like,

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:20.067
"Oh, it's like two turntables.
We're going back and forth."

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:22.634
-It really was, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.534
-We did --
We did history of rap.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.901
-It was history of rap
done with the actual --

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:31.534
-But with the actual people!
I was texting Justin Timberlake,

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.200
like, "Are you watching this,
man? Come on!"

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.334
[ Laughter ]
It was unbelievable.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.601
I just want to say
congratulations.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.267
You should be so proud.
That was unbelievable.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:42.133
It was bigger
than a Super Bowl performance.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:45.133
It was bigger than anything.
You crushed it.

